{
  "id": "card-get-reviews",
  "title": "getCard and listCardReviews: schedule cache of a new, a reviewed and a deleted card; history newest first, undone rows included, history of a deleted card",
  "covers": [
    "cards.get",
    "cards.get_deleted_410",
    "cards.reviews_newest_first",
    "cards.reviews_undone_included",
    "cards.reviews_deleted_card"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "Three cards: ...10 graduated with Easy 60 days ago (one review in the log), ...20 is new, ...30 graduated the same way and was deleted yesterday (card.deleted; its note is live).",
    "Step 0: card 10 is in state review with reps 1. Step 1: card 20 is new: every schedule property is null, reps 0.",
    "Step 2: the history of card 10 is its one seeded review, next_cursor null. Step 3: a card never answered has an empty history.",
    "Step 4 answers card 10 Good; step 5 answers card 20 Again (it becomes a learning card).",
    "Step 6: the history of card 10 is newest first: this device's answer, then the seeded review.",
    "Step 7: limit=1 returns the newest row and a cursor. /next_cursor is ignored: a cursor is an opaque string and the shell's need not equal the server's; only the rows are compared. (Following a cursor is therefore not parity-tested.)",
    "Steps 8-9: the cards' schedule cache after the answers (reps 2; learning with reps 1).",
    "Step 10 undoes the answer of step 4. Step 11: the undone row is still in the history, first, with undone_at set (the golden holds the instant); the seeded row is not undone. Step 12: card 10 is back to reps 1.",
    "Step 13: a deleted card is 410 gone; step 14: with include_deleted=true it is returned. Step 15: its history is still served (history is never deleted).",
    "Steps 16-17: an id that exists nowhere is 404 for both operations."
  ],
